{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/memcached","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:10.789Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/cbl-mariner/base/memcached/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/cbl-mariner/base/memcached/about"},"readme":"***Warning: Azure Linux 2.0 will reach its End of Life (EOL) on July 31st, 2025. After this date, it will no longer receive updates, security patches, or support, which could leave your systems vulnerable. We strongly recommend upgrading to an Azure Linux 3.0 image before July 31st, 2025.***\n\n## About\n\nThis repository contains the official Memcached image for CBL-Mariner.\n\n### What is CBL-Mariner?\n\nCBL-Mariner is an internal Linux distribution for Microsoft’s cloud infrastructure and edge products and services. CBL-Mariner is designed to provide a consistent platform for these devices and services and will enhance Microsoft’s ability to stay current on Linux updates.  \n\nTo learn more about CBL-Mariner, refer to our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n### What is Memcached?\n\nMemcached is an service that provides distributed hashmaps.\n\nSee: [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memcached](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memcached)\n\n## Featured tags\n\n- `1`\n- `1-cm2.0`\n\nThe featured tags are multi-architecture tags (i.e., `x86-64` and `aarch64`) that refer to the latest version of the image. Additional tags that are specific to Memcached version, Mariner build, or architecture can be found in the Tags section.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Running a `memcached` server locally\n\n`1.` Run the CBL-Mariner `memcached` container image with an exposed port for access.\n\n    docker run -d -p <host port>:11211 mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/memcached:1\n\nThe default container startup command is `memcached` with the user `memcache`. This launches `memcached` with the user `memcache`.\n\n### Launch Mariner shell\n\nThe Memcached image ships with a bash shell. The launch command can be provided to docker run command to launch Mariner shell. The following command will launch the shell:\n\n    docker run -it mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/memcached:1 /bin/bash\n\n## Support\n\nCBL-Mariner container images are supported only for internal Microsoft use. For more information please see our [Support Statement](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/2.0/SUPPORT.md).\n\n## License\n\nThe CBL-Mariner distribution is provided under the [MIT license](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/2.0/LICENSE). Individual packages and components are governed by their own licenses included in the package sources available via srpm on [packages.microsoft.com](https://packages.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/) or via our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-07-21T16:46:10.2551945+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"MIT","links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"89K+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"1.6-cm2.0","digest":"sha256:a4fc437d36d1b4e280a928ab9a72db2103523b4e0cff103bfaceec53159380db","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:06:21.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"1.6","digest":"sha256:a4fc437d36d1b4e280a928ab9a72db2103523b4e0cff103bfaceec53159380db","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:06:12.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"1-cm2.0","digest":"sha256:a4fc437d36d1b4e280a928ab9a72db2103523b4e0cff103bfaceec53159380db","pushed":"2026-03-12T21:0